              # workspace</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span>├── crates/</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span>│   ├── domain/                # types, no I/O — fully unit-testable</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span>│   ├── api/                   # axum server</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span>│   └── worker/                # background jobs</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span>├── migrations/</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span>├── .env.example</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span>└── web/                       # Next.js dashboard</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span>    ├── app/</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span>    │   ├── layout.tsx</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span>    │   ├── page.tsx</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span>    │   └── globals.css</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span>    └── components/</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>The <code>domain</code> crate has no database, no HTTP and no async — so its tests run in\nmicroseconds and its API is the contract everything else builds on.</p>\n<h2 id=\"milestones\">Milestones</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Milestone</th>\n<th>Done when</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Schema + migrations</td>\n<td><code>sqlx migrate run</code> succeeds on a fresh DB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Ingest endpoint</td>\n<td><code>curl</code> with an API key inserts an event</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Dashboard endpoint</td>\n<td>returns the JSON above from seeded data</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>Worker rollups</td>\n<td><code>usage_daily</code> fills for yesterday</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>Next.js dashboard</td>\n<td>renders real data with HeroUI</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>Deploy</td>\n<td>container runs, <code>/readyz</code> green, migrations on boot</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Build them in this order. Each one is independently demonstrable, which matters\nwhen you are learning: a half-finished milestone is still a working system.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Next:</strong> <a href=\"02-rust-api-build.md\">Building the Rust API</a></p>"}